"comparison": "Both Bank of America (BAC) and Citigroup (C) define consolidation of VIEs based on the dual criteria of power to direct significant activities and the obligation/right to absorb significant losses or benefits. BAC explicitly states it consolidates if it has control over initial design or manages assets AND absorbs significant gains/losses ('bac_2024_8_P091_S001'). Similarly, Citi consolidates a VIE when it has both the power to direct activities that most significantly impact economic performance and a right to receive benefits or obligation to absorb losses that could be potentially significant ('c_2024_8_P013_S001'). BAC provides specific examples where it does NOT consolidate (e.g., CDOs where it is not collateral manager), while Citi's candidate disclosure provides general criteria but also illustrates non-consolidation of agency securitizations due to lack of power ('c_2024_8_P644_S002').",
