"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both BAC and Goldman Sachs (GS) apply the standard primary beneficiary test for VIE consolidation, requiring both power to direct significant activities and the obligation to absorb losses or right to receive benefits. BAC notes it consolidates customer investment vehicles if it controls initial design/manages assets and absorbs significant gains/losses ('bac_2024_8_P091_S001'). GS states it has a controlling financial interest in a VIE when it has variable interests providing (i) power to direct activities that most significantly impact economic performance and (ii) obligation to absorb losses or right to receive benefits that could potentially be significant ('gs_2024_8_P047_S003'). The core accounting principle regarding the dual thresholds for consolidation is identical.",
