"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both BAC and Morgan Stanley (MS) address the specific context of CDOs and servicing/management rights. BAC states it generally does not consolidate CDOs because it does not routinely serve as collateral manager (lacking power to direct significant activities), but consolidates if it becomes a majority senior holder after default and acquires power to manage assets ('bac_2024_8_P090_S002', 'bac_2024_8_P090_S003'). MS similarly states it does not consolidate securitizations or CDOs for which it does not act as servicer or collateral manager, considering these roles as representing the power to make significant economic decisions, unless it holds other rights ('ms_2024_8_P427_S003'). Both peers highlight that lacking specific management/servicing power is a key reason for non-consolidation of these specific VIE structures.",
